  {
   "type": "h1",
   "text": "1. La forma"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "El past simple (pasado) de un verbo regular se forma con <b>-ed</b>. Buena noticia: la forma es <b>igual para todas las personas</b>. Nada de seis terminaciones como en español: <i>trabajé, trabajaste, trabajó</i> = <b>worked</b>."
  },
  {
   "type": "conj",
   "verb": "to work",
   "meaning": "trabajar",
   "label": "verbo regular",
   "tense": "past simple",
   "forms": [
    "work*ed*",
    "work*ed*",
    "work*ed*",
    "work*ed*",
    "work*ed*",
    "work*ed*"
   ],
   "examples": [
    [
     "I worked late yesterday.",
     "Ayer trabajé hasta tarde."
    ],
    [
     "You worked very hard last year.",
     "El año pasado trabajaste muchísimo."
    ],
    [
     "She worked in Paris in 2019.",
     "Ella trabajó en París en 2019."
    ],
    [
     "We worked together for five years.",
     "Trabajamos juntos cinco años."
    ],
    [
     "You worked on Saturday.",
     "Trabajasteis el sábado."
    ],
    [
     "They worked at the same school.",
     "Trabajaban en el mismo colegio."
